- `results/semisynth.parquet` (`summarise_c7.py` from `c7.jsonl`; `fit_semisynth.py`, `run_c7.py`): C7. Generator logit P = mu + a_i + b_k + U_i . V_k fitted on the pool (rank 20, l2 0.005 from rank {1, 3, 5, 8, 12, 20} x l2 {0.001, 0.005, 0.02} by held-out log-likelihood on 10% masked cells, -0.1207; the rank is at the grid's upper edge but the likelihood is flat beyond about 12). `kind`: `validation_split_half` (fit on half A, prediction for the half-B pool size, measured on half B items outside S), `extrapolation` (fit with 75 of 128 configurations, predict all 128), `misspec` (dependence `mode` fitted / indep / equicorr), `curve` (fit on all items, K up to 512, n up to 800). 3 seeds (`seed`; -1 = mean over seeds), 10 generated worlds per prediction, 400 draws per measured cell; `real_value` with `lo`/`hi` = item-bootstrap percentile interval centred on the measured value, Monte-Carlo noise of 40 draws per replicate included (conservative; the interval is about 0.039 wide, so `inside` is a weak test and does not tell the three dependence modes apart; the MC-free interval is in `measured_lo_mcfree/hi_mcfree`). Predicted gap inside the interval in 24/24 (split half), 23/24 (extrapolation), 24/24 / 24/24 / 23/24 (fitted / indep / equicorr); predicted minus measured +0.0035 (split half), +0.0009 (extrapolation): the generator overstates the gap by about 6%. Curves: lower-bound coverage max-t 0.96-0.99, Bonferroni 0.99-1.00 (`coverage_maxt`, `coverage_bonferroni`); `inside_support` is False for n > 200 or K > 128.
- `results/matrix_facts.parquet` (`matrix_facts.py`, `matrix_facts_table.py`): Tab 1 facts of the pool: 1500 items, 128 configurations, accuracy mean 0.274 (range 0.205-0.303), sigma_theta 0.0141 (pool-bootstrap CI 0.0118-0.0186), mean pairwise item correlation of the configurations 0.656, letter-bias share 0.17, `delta_leak` 0.42 (CI 0.22-0.62, an item bootstrap over only 9 probe items: a small probe, not a rate).

- `results/real_tool.parquet`, `results/real_tool_draws.parquet`, raw `results/real_tool_w*.jsonl` (`run_c8.py`, `summarise_c8.py`): C8, the real tool. Tool = the `dspy` package's own `BootstrapFewShotWithRandomSearch` (dspy 3.0.4; 16 candidate sets, i.e. 19 programs counting zero-shot, labels-only and unshuffled; 2 bootstrapped and 2 labeled demonstrations), run live with the study's scorer as its language model (`analysis/dspy_lm.py`, direct-answer letter log-probabilities), trainset = valset = S, n = |S| = 60 pool items, 24 draws of S (draw index = seed), pool = the 1500 items, Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct. Per draw: `reported` = the selected program's accuracy on S as the tool computed it, `truth` = its accuracy on 400 random pool items outside S (SE 0.023 each; `truth_se`), `gap` = reported - truth, `leak_part` = reported minus the score on S without the selected program's own demonstration items (`reported_leak_free`, `gap_leak_free`: a demonstration drawn from S is scored on itself), `pred_kappa` = the equal-theta search-log predictor on the 19 x 60 score matrix the tool computed. `real_tool.parquet` (24 draws, `status = tested`): mean reported 0.357, mean truth 0.291, **mean gap 0.0662 (t-interval over the draws, `ci_kind = draw-spread-t`, 0.0393-0.0931; SD over draws 0.064; 20 of 24 draws positive)**; leak-free gap 0.048 (0.021-0.075), the leakage part 0.018; the predictor `pred_kappa` 0.054 = 0.82 x the gap (the tool's gap is above the predictor by 0.012, and the leak-free gap is below it); zero-shot is the selected program in 8% of draws and the maximum is tied in 1.7 programs on average (ties are broken by the tool's order). **Verdict, by the rule fixed in experiment-repo#2 before the result: `not consistent`.** The rule: the tool's mean gap inside the pool-bootstrap interval of the replay gap of random search with B = 20 at n = 60 on the matrix, 0.0515-0.0647 (replay gap 0.0581; `replay_lo/hi`). The tool's mean gap 0.0662 is 0.0015 above the upper end, so the rule says not consistent. Beside it, not used for the verdict: the replay interval of the corrected `total_ci` intervals (0.0491-0.0672; `replay_lo_total/hi_total`) contains 0.0662 (`inside_total_ci = True`), and the tool's own interval (0.039-0.093) contains the replay gap (`c8_interval_contains_replay_gap`). The tool's gap is above the replay's by 0.008 (0.066 against 0.058) with a standard error of 0.013 on the tool's mean: the data neither separate the two nor establish that they are equal. Read it as the real tool's optimism being of the replay's size and nominally slightly larger, with demonstration leakage (0.018) as one identified contributor. The `replay_*` columns say which interval is which.

## Runtimes and compute used
Measured. Compute charged by the world to this repository's jobs (`ht-resource status local-compute`, `used.spend`): 1,122,124 CPU-seconds = 311.7 CPU-hours, jobs of 4 CPUs each on a CPU-only host, **including** work that was lost: the first C8 launch (all 8 jobs killed for memory, exit 137), jobs ended at the 4-hour limit, and draws computed twice by two workers. The matrix (18 workers) took 187,354 s of worker wall time summed. C8: 24 draws, each 3,800-5,300 s wall (mean 4,293 s; 103,039 s summed) with 8 to 9 jobs sharing the host, 39,189 calls of the dspy language model (1,601-1,692 per draw) and 67,833 distinct (program prefix, item) forward passes of the studied model over the 24 draws (memoised: a repeated prompt is not run twice). The token count of the C8 forward passes was not logged and is not reported; the matrix's is in `matrix_tokens.json`.

